      "text": "my blood … shed for many for the remission of sins, Matt. 26:28 (D&C 27:2). John did … preach the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins, Mark 1:4 (D&C 33:11). salvation … by the remission of their sins, Luke 1:77. baptism of repentance for the remission of sins, Luke 3:3 (Moro. 8:11; D&C 19:31; 107:20). repentance and remission of sins should be preached, Luke 24:47 (Moro. 3:3). Whose soever sins ye remit, they are remitted, John 20:23 (D&C 132:46). Repent, and be baptized … for the remission of sins, Acts 2:38. believeth in him shall receive remission of sins, Acts 10:43 (Mosiah 3:13). his righteousness for the remission of sins, Rom. 3:25. without shedding of blood is no remission, Heb. 9:22. where remission of these is, there is no more offering, Heb. 10:18.",
